Striking result. Let me analyze: the prime indicator's TT bond dimension hits **exactly 2^{d-j-1}+1 at every cut past the middle** — exactly half the maximum possible plus one. Compare random data which sits at full bound. This is not random!

The reason is a small calculation: at unfolding level `j`, row `i ≥ 1` represents block `[i·2^{d-j}+1, (i+1)·2^{d-j}]`, which for `i ≥ 1` always begins at an even base, so all odd-column entries become even values > 2 and vanish. Half the columns are forced zero. That's an exact, provable factor-2 compression — and no more. Let me write up.
